 "text": "Sound: the 80s synth-pop drum machine: a firm kick on 1 and 3, a snare and clap together on 2 and 4 in a big, bright room, steady eighth hats. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 118. Kick from a Sequencer on eighths (steps 1 and 5, plus 6 for a little push); a snare and a clap both from another Sequencer on 3 and 7, layered; hats on every eighth. A large Reverb on everything (the 80s big-room drum sound).\n\nTweak: the reverb's SIZE and MIX, the clap's level, TEMPO.",
